{"id": "EUVD-2026-97700", "enisaUuid": "554c2f3e-2a81-3280-984c-77124c222516", "description": "FreeRDP 3.10.0 through 3.32.2 contains a heap buffer overflow in the WinPR png_write_data callback that writes past the buffer after a realloc failure. A malicious RDP clipboard peer can supply a large CF_DIB image that triggers out-of-bounds memcpy during PNG conversion, causing a client crash.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:38:15", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-wf3x-658c-52m5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.10.0-through-3.32.2-heap-buffer-overflow-in-winpr-png-conversion"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109256", "GHSA-h8f2-6xfm-5cjf"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f1df7b69-aa6c-36dc-8b68-802a7ac699dc", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.10.0 \u22643.32.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8077e6b1-2df3-35c8-a91d-34e288c367dc", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}